<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Tryavna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1190">1190</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uprising-of-asen-and-peter">Uprising of Asen and Peter</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Tryavna was fought in 1190 in a pass of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkan-mountains">Balkan Mountains</a> near Tryavna, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>. The Bulgarian leaders Asen and Peter ambushed the army of the Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isaac-ii-angelos">Isaac II Angelos</a> as it withdrew from a failed siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veliko-tarnovo">Tarnovo</a>, and the emperor barely escaped. The defeat ended Byzantine attempts to crush the Bulgarian revolt and secured the restored Bulgarian state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tryavna.jpg" alt="Battle of Tryavna" width="320" height="382" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kandi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Tryavna_Pass.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
